## 18. Baseline chronology and selection diagnosis

The later generated-field study has actual8D/384D/768D numerical fits; do not treat its earlier zero-ready768 preparation as the current historical frontier. A direct saved-result read confirms width768/seed2718 final candidates at42/48 exact development outputs for two arms,41/48 for the every2 arm, with all18 fits still selecting epoch0. Exact saved-artifact identities and fields are in the research report. No model was replayed.

Consequences for the first experiment:

1. Preserve chronological baseline identities. The early0/48 gradient study is a useful mechanistic-diagnostic source, not the strongest known output baseline.
2. Include the stronger later candidate family as a potential comparator only after current-source/checkpoint eligibility is established. Do not assert that a new method improves over previous work by comparing only against the weaker early fit.
3. Keep the original selected checkpoint distinct from the last attempted state and the best diagnostic candidate. Report all three where available; use none of them as a newly promoted model without admission.
4. Diagnose the selection frontier separately: epoch0's low extra-rule count can coexist with unusable/no valid outputs, while a trained candidate improves coverage and still violates an unchanged extra-rule gate. Report syntax, complete coverage, missing/extra whole-rule content, facets, retention, exactness and cost together.
5. Never remove an old criterion to pass an experiment. A proposed alternative development selector requires a new version, prospective criteria, independent review and untouched evaluation data. It must not change legal/corpus admission or retrofit approval to the historical42/48 outputs.
6. Test every2 or other auxiliary cadence against fixed-compute and fixed-example controls separately. Reducing supervision exposure can reduce time without improving convergence. Count source-only collection, graph replay, retry work and failed attempts.
7. Do not pool the repeated48 development cases as independent observations. Use dependency-grouped new heldout data for any new generalization or convergence claim.

This is now a two-part research question: what improves source-faithful learning, and which predeclared selector can recognize a useful qualified candidate without rewarding empty output or overlooking harmful errors? Neither is solved by decreasing CE alone.

## 19. Feasibility and causal-hypothesis gates before new optimization

Later source-head results strengthen the candidate baseline to47/48 exact development outputs for two384D final attempts and46/48,45/48 for768D attempts. The selected states remain separate, including one epoch52 state with14/48 exact and161 missing rules. See the research report for inspected saved-artifact identities, retained guardian failure, and limits. No new convergence result is claimed.

### Effective-input identifiability

Before optimizing, group examples by the exact information actually observable to the selected decoder after preprocessing: source bytes, permitted governing context, embeddings, masks, transforms, prefix availability, and selected interpretation. Inspect TRAIN only when diagnosing curriculum/fit. Do not inspect heldout target labels to choose a recipe.

If an observable input is identical but genuinely incompatible accepted meanings require different outputs, the route lacks an input distinction or an explicit output-set contract. No optimization method can choose a uniquely correct deterministic answer from unavailable information. Equivalent formalizations, multiple accepted targets, and unknown interpretations must not be mislabeled as contradictions merely because serialized targets differ.

Embedding collisions alone are not a whole-decoder impossibility result when raw text or other context remains available. Conversely, distinct vectors do not establish that a finite selected head can separate labels or learn them within budget. Repeat checks at the actual float precision and normalization used by the decoder.

### Expressivity and output completeness

Check that the chosen codec, target grammar, context ceiling and complete output budget can express the entire selected norm, including conditions, exceptions and definitions. A one-rule decoder or fixed-array classifier cannot qualify by deleting difficult clauses. An output-cap experiment with unchanged short targets measures stopping/readout behavior, not long-target learning.

### Testable hypotheses and matched controls

| Hypothesis | Existing evidence motivating it | Proposed discriminating comparison | Claims it cannot establish alone |
|---|---|---|---|
| Training exposure or optimizer groups limit8D readout | Probe/full-decoder exposure and rate differences | Equal clause/token exposure with matched optimizer and shrinkage; preserve all other losses | Fresh legal generalization or representation equivalence |
| Recurrent/prefix pathway overrides correct source fields | Perfect raw larger-width readouts coexist with generated action errors | Exact observed prefix/state tracing, sham versus localized intervention, full-vocabulary outputs and independent fidelity | A probe score is not proof of causal use |
| Shared objectives conflict near curriculum transition | Exact replay localizes token-dominated spikes | Replay original state; examine shared-parameter gradients; separately controlled objective/clip interventions | Spike magnitude alone does not identify a recurrent-Jacobian cause |
| Auxiliary cadence improves total efficiency | Every2 historical arms reduce cost and exposure | Equal-compute and equal-exposure comparisons with all retry/generation costs | Fixed-update fit time is not fastest convergence |
| Bounded boundary edits improve adaptation | Existing donor-copy/new-boundary warm start | Same donor and input profile, bounded edit versus gradient/random/rule controls, equal selection budget | Raw deltas do not transfer across unrelated architectures |
| Structured policy credit helps residual decisions | Existing generated-site diagnostics can localize observed errors | Independently verified action scores and outcomes; policy baseline versus declared credit method | Reference-prefix teacher forcing is not autonomous policy rollout |

These hypotheses are proposed, not explanations already proved. Use the unchanged current gates for acceptance. Any prospective development-selector alternative needs independent versioning and review and cannot change legal admission.

### Resource and state feasibility

Audit selected current checkpoint, complete tokenizer prompts/labels, model/optimizer precision, full state footprint, output/storage budget, runtime import identity, and closure under the existing owners before an admitted fit. Preserve explicit fresh-optimizer versus exact-resume semantics. Repairing a lifecycle failure requires its own qualification; successful numerical outputs do not erase an original guardian failure.

